      "script": "My coworker presented my work as his own while I was out sick. He copied the deck from our shared project folder, removed my name, and told our director he had built the entire strategy over the weekend. I came back Monday to congratulations directed at the wrong desk. I did not argue. I asked to join the follow-up meeting because I had “a few implementation notes.” In the conference room, he stumbled through questions about the numbers, so the director asked me to explain. I opened version history on the projector. Every slide showed my account creating it, plus his account making one edit: deleting my name. Nobody spoke for a few seconds. The director ended the meeting, reassigned the project to me, and asked him to document his contribution. His document was one sentence long. By Friday, I was promoted to lead, and he was assigned to take meeting notes.",
