      "script": "My neighbor decided the public curb in front of his house belonged to him. Every morning, he placed two orange cones there before leaving for work, then shouted at anyone who moved them. After he blocked my visiting nurse from parking, I asked him once to stop. He told me to “call the city if you care so much.” So I did. Parking enforcement explained that abandoned objects in the roadway could be collected, but they needed a complaint each time. For one week, I photographed the cones from my porch and filed the same short report before breakfast. A city truck arrived every afternoon and removed them. He kept buying replacements: first cheap cones, then weighted cones, then cones with his address painted underneath. The truck took those too. On Friday, an officer handed him a citation for obstructing the roadway. He finally stopped reserving the curb. The city storage yard now owns his entire cone collection.",
